---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Cascadia Systems">
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="hero-topo section bg-gradient-to-b from-dark-bg via-dark-surface to-dark-bg">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl">
        <h1 class="mb-8 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">
          I build the systems that replace the work your staff does by hand.
        </h1>
        <div class="space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
          <p>
            I'm Devin MacArthur, a data-systems engineer in Portland. For the last few years my
            day job has been keeping a statewide membership organization's data moving between
            the places it lives: a Salesforce-based CRM, an older membership database that
            predates it, SharePoint, a payment processor, an election platform, and the
            spreadsheets people maintain by hand because nothing else will. Almost everything I've
            built there started as a task somebody did every week and hated.
          </p>
          <p>
            Cascadia Systems is where I do that work for other organizations. The offer is
            narrow on purpose. I spend thirty days with you, find out where the hours actually go,
            automate the worst of it so that it runs on a schedule without me, and write down what
            I would do next. It costs $12,000. Details are on the <a href="/services/" class="link">services page</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-10 flex flex-col gap-4 sm:flex-row">
          <a href="/contact/" class="btn btn-primary">Email me</a>
          <a href="/services/" class="btn btn-secondary">What the thirty days look like</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Examples -->
  <section class="section border-t border-dark-border">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl">
        <h2 class="mb-8 text-3xl font-bold">Some things I've built, with the names filed off</h2>
        <div class="space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
          <p>
            A membership organization was getting scanned paper applications and paying people to
            retype them. I built an extractor that reads the scan, pulls the fields into a
            structured record, checks them against the rules the staff already applied in their
            heads, and sends anything it isn't sure about to a person instead of guessing.
          </p>
          <p>
            The same organization's payment processor stopped forwarding card transactions and
            nobody upstream noticed for six weeks. I found it by matching bank deposits against
            the membership system, line by line, which is a tedious thing to do once and a
            trivial thing to do every night. It runs every night now.
          </p>
          <p>
            A financial analysis that an analyst used to build by hand, one workbook per district
            for every district in the state, now fills itself in from the state's published data.
            The analyst still does the analysis. He just doesn't do the typing.
          </p>
          <p>
            None of these took more than a few weeks. The hard part in each case was not the
            code. It was sitting with the person who did the job long enough to understand what
            they were actually checking for, which is never what the procedure document says.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Limits -->
  <section class="section bg-dark-surface">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl">
        <h2 class="mb-8 text-3xl font-bold">What I'm not</h2>
        <div class="space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
          <p>
            I'm one person. Until early 2027 I'm doing this alongside a full-time job, which means
            I take on one or two engagements at a time and I'm honest about scheduling. I don't
            hand work to subcontractors, so what you get is me, and what you don't get is a
            team. If you need a platform rebuilt by six engineers, I'm the wrong call, and I can
            usually tell you who the right one is.
          </p>
          <p>
            I also won't sell you AI for its own sake. A fair number of the processes I look at
            need a scheduled script and a shared table, not a model. When that's the answer I'll
            say so, and the thirty days will cost the same.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Data -->
  <section class="section border-t border-dark-border">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl">
        <h2 class="mb-8 text-3xl font-bold">Where your data goes</h2>
        <div class="space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
          <p>
            Nowhere, if I can help it. I start with read-only access and ask for write access only
            to the one thing I'm automating. If the data is sensitive, the processing runs on your
            machines or on hardware I own in Portland, with no outside model provider in the loop.
            When a hosted model is the right tool I'll name the provider, show you the
            data-processing agreement, and put it in the scope in writing. At the end I rotate
            every credential back to you and delete my working copies. I'll put that in writing too.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="section bg-dark-surface">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl">
        <h2 class="mb-6 text-3xl font-bold">If this sounds like your problem</h2>
        <p class="mb-8 text-lg text-text-secondary">
          Email me a paragraph about the process that costs you the most time. Thirty minutes on
          a call is enough for both of us to know whether it's a fit.
        </p>
        <a href="/contact/" class="btn btn-primary">devin.macarthur@cascadiasystems.org</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
